I recently installed a U.S. Robotics Sportster 28.8/33.6
external modem (PlugNPlay) on my Alpha AXP 150 running
Windows NT 4.0 beta 2.  I connected it to COM2 using the
control panel.  I then downloaded a 3MB file from a
company bulletin board using the new HyperTerminal
applet with throughput of 33200 bps.  I also used some
Galacticomm GUI software for the BBS which ran in 486
emulator mode.  I still got very reasonable throughput.  I am
very delighted with this solution which did not require any ISA
config tweaking with the ECU.

