From jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com Tue Jul  2 14:35:20 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <c=US%a=_%p=Digital%l=NTMAIL2-960702185004Z-17506@ntmail4.zso.dec.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jul 1996 11:50:04 -0700
From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: Alpha AXP 150 dual boot

Benedito,

You will already have a system partition on your AXP 150, e.g., 

	scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2),

with a directory like, e.g.,

	\os\winnt351,

in which are stored hal.dll, osloader.exe, and *.pal.  You must create
another such directory in the same partition, e.g.,

	\os\winnt40,

into which Setup will put the NT 4.0 hal.dll, osloader.exe, and *.pal. 
Your boot selection for this version of NT will look like, assuming you
have made your system partition the second on the volume,

  SYSTEMPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)
  OSLOADER=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)\os\winnt40\osloader.exe
  ...

Be sure you don't try to keep a single "os\winnt" subdirectory, since
the hal.dll and osloader.exe files required by each version of NT are
different.

Cheers,
James

