I've found Emulex NetJet cards to be excellent network printer 
interfaces.  They provide better protocol support than HP Jetdirect cards 
and provide a better mechanism for configuration.   In addition to having 
a graphical configuration utility similar to JetAdmin,  They also provide 
a command-line interface reachable via telnet or lat/mop that closely 
resembles a terminal server interface.   They provide both internal cards 
for HP laserjets and external adapters for any parallel or serial printer.

No affiliation with Emulex,  just personal experience.  

