Hello, all.

Later this week, there will probably be a network transition at garply.
With any luck, no one on the outside will even notice the change from one
service provider to another.  However, I for one am not holding my breath
(an American-ism for "don't expect it to happen that way").  My ex-partner
had not even decided on a network configuration or purchased the hardware
required as of Monday, so I think he'll be hard pressed to make a successful
transition.  (One of the many reasons why he's an "ex-", but that's another
can of worms!)

Given the instability of the network and service here, I am working with
others to establish a new site for all the Web pages (more to come), mail
list, and file archives, with significantly improved bandwidth and much
more processing power behing the scenes.  In order to make all this a reality,
I need some help, and am approaching all of you for a volunteer.

The workload of managing the mail list is significantly higher than I
originally expected.  My original scope for the mail list was on the order
of a few dozen users informally chatting about Alphas and NT.  When we passed
the 300 user mark, I knew I was in over my head, and we're now at over 750
and still climbing.  The workload has completely usurped my time from doing
the other things that I originally started doing with this site -- finding and
distributing Alpha NT applications and creating Web pages in support of Alpha
NT (just take a look at the last date the file archive was updated for proof of
how misdirected I've been!).

Perhaps it is the way I've approached management of the mail list (I am a
complete and self-admitted majordomo-newbie), or perhaps I've overlooked
something simple, but I need some help.  Would someone be interested in
taking over the day to day administrative tasks associated with the mail list
(e.g., subscribing members, tracking bounced messages, etc.)?  There is
no renumeration involved, nor other rewards other than the self-satisfaction
that you are helping your fellow AlphaNT'ers and an occasional "AttaPerson"  
(P.C. attaboy).  I would hope someone knowledgable with mail lists and
their administration is available and willing, but would consider another
novice.

Volunteers can try emailing me at this address (aaron@garply.com) or at my
work address (asakovich@ncs.com).  Even if you've got a question or some
other suggestions, as always, I enjoy hearing from you.

Thanks for your time, support, and patronage.  Long live AlphaNT!

Regards,
Aaron

