> is a very big problem for me if this is true.
> 
> Thanks inadvance for any help
> 
> Clarence Satchell (Satchell_CE@Corning.com)
> 
> 

I just did some testing.
On NT-Server 3.51 sp4 it is like this:
If a Mac opens the file first a NT workstation can't access the file (used by 
another process) havn't check if another Mac can access it.
If a NTWS opens it first a Mac can open it to. If the NTWS closes the file it 
can't reopen it (used by another process).
The same problem appears regardless if you have read only or full control 
permissions to the file/directory.

I never had a question about opening a copy of the file, but if I try to save 
a file which is read only I get the question to save with a diffrent 
name/location (Save as dialogue).

With a NT-Server 3.50 sp2 there where no problems opening the documents with a 
Mac or a NTWS in any order.

