Subject: Autodesk's Commitment to AlphaNT...

hi.
        I have just spent the last two days in various meetings with
        people from Digital and Kinetix (formerly Autodesk's Multimedia
        division) and the word is not very promising.  Here at UCLA 
        we use Autocad r.13 on the Alpha's and it is great, but we have
        been dying to get our hands on the 3D Studio Max for AlphaNT.
        We have heard all sorts of stories but no real answers.

        Apparently, Autodesk doesn't perceive a need to complete the
        port in progress to the Alphas,  and they have even tried to 
        convince me that the Alphas weren't fast enough.  I have not
        heard Intel offering a 500 mhz Panything!  It is my hope that
        through this Post, I will encourage any AlphaNT user that 
        could benefit from using 3D Studio Max, to express their 
        great disappointment in Autodesk and Kinetix's commitment
        to the AlphaNT market.

        My personal contact at Kinetix is Ronni Banks.
        His Email address is:   Ronni.Banks@autodesk.com
                                                 415-507-6221
        
        I have not been signed into NDA secrecy yet, but some folks at
        Digital are working on getting us an eval copy of the Fabled 
        FX!32 such that we may test the emulation situation to run the
        Intel NT version of 3D Studio Max.  My contacts at Digital could
        not speak concretely about any knowledge of such a test having
        happened already.  If anyone has already tested this matching
        of products already, and cannot post freely their results due to the
        NDA,   Please Contact your FX!32 representative or my contact
        at Digital, Paul Lawson.

        His Stats:   Paul.Lawson@ivo.mts.dec.com
                                714-261-4478

        

        3D Studio Max looks very good, but it is far from the only game in
        town.  I have been quite impressed with the performance of
        Lightwave and I am still exploring the Intergraph/Bentley family of
        Software with Modeller and Masterpiece although I have no hands
        on experience with Masterpiece.  The Bentley package looks
        especially good for any educational institutions as the basic package
        price independent of Platform is $250.00 per seat for the 4 app
        combo of Microstation, Modeller, PowerDraft and Masterpiece.  
        We pay about that much for each copy of each application from Autodesk.

        And the Bentley products run on all common platforms including but not
        limited to DEC AlphaNT, Intel, PowerPC etc...

        I work with another fellow who is a die hard PoorerPC user, but I am 
        always amazed at the support that his various mailings lists similiar
        to this, are able to drum up in support of their platform.  They are 
        fanatical when it comes to software not being available for their
        systems.  I think we could develop a slightly stronger voice to some of
        the software companies.  I must admit however, that I really appreciate
        the seemingly secret backdoor that we have with Digital and Microsoft
        through this list.  I have been VERY pleased with the speed and accuracy
        of the posts from those companies.  Keep up the good work!

        It is getting a little slippery on this box...

