From: Aaron Bauch <abauch@email2.hlo.dec.com>
Subject: Re: EV4-EV5 upgrade

The HAL for each hardware system is unique in Windows NT.  Since
you changed the CPU section of your system you have created a "new"
configuration of the base hardware.

The HAL is loaded when the OS is installed and the cleanest way to
install the HAL you need is probably to "upgrade" your operating
system by doing a new install over your existing NT, of the same
version in the same directory.  It should not destroy anything
else but will install the correct HAL for the system you are now running
(I think).  The worst that it will do is re-install the same HAL
that you already have if it checks a configuration file that
tells it you still have a 21064.  The HAL for all of the versions of
the 2100 is on the Microsoft distrinution CD for NT so you shouldn't
even need a separate HAL floppy.

Good luck.

Aaron

